From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 03:31:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] chore(ffi): drop unused create_client binding and test GVL
 release

create_client_from_uri already releases the GVL (blocking: true was added
in #316), but nothing guarded that behaviour, and the byte-based
create_client binding was never called anywhere.

- Remove the dead Valkey::Bindings.create_client attach_function; clients
  are only created through create_client_from_uri.
- Add a server-free unit test that connects to a local listener which
  never answers and asserts an unrelated Ruby thread keeps running while
  Valkey.new waits for connect_timeout. The test fails if blocking: true
  is removed from create_client_from_uri.

Closes #309

Signed-off-by: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 CHANGELOG.md                     |  1 +
 lib/valkey/bindings.rb           |  9 ++-----
 test/unit/connection_gvl_test.rb | 42 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 45 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 test/unit/connection_gvl_test.rb

diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 422647e..95ee945 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@
 * fix(ruby): release the GVL while a client connects. `create_client` and `create_client_from_uri` were declared without `blocking: true`, so client creation held the GVL for the whole call and stalled every other Ruby thread until it returned; this affects all clients, not only Pub/Sub ones ([#316](https://github.com/valkey-io/valkey-glide-ruby/pull/316))
 * fix(ruby): resp now defaults to core behavior, which is resp3. This is the same as other GLIDE clients ([#331](https://github.com/valkey-io/valkey-glide-ruby/pull/331))
 * fix(ruby): size the per-argument length buffer passed to glide-ffi by the platform's `unsigned long` width instead of a hardcoded 8 bytes, which wrote past the buffer on platforms with a 4-byte `unsigned long` ([#338](https://github.com/valkey-io/valkey-glide-ruby/pull/338))
+* chore(ruby): remove the unused `Valkey::Bindings.create_client` FFI binding (clients are created only through `create_client_from_uri`) and add a server-free regression test asserting that `Valkey.new` releases the GVL while connecting ([#309](https://github.com/valkey-io/valkey-glide-ruby/issues/309))
 
 ### Changes
 
diff --git a/lib/valkey/bindings.rb b/lib/valkey/bindings.rb
index 634859f..9b9b8e5 100644
--- a/lib/valkey/bindings.rb
+++ b/lib/valkey/bindings.rb
@@ -235,13 +235,8 @@ class Valkey
       :pointer, :long   # pattern + length
     ], :void
 
-    attach_function :create_client, [
-      :pointer,        # *const u8 (connection_request_bytes)
-      :ulong,          # usize (connection_request_len)
-      ClientType.by_ref, # *const ClientType
-      :pubsub_callback # callback
-    ], :pointer, blocking: true # *const ConnectionResponse
-
+    # blocking: true releases the GVL while glide-core connects (and retries),
+    # so other Ruby threads keep running during `Valkey.new` (issue #309).
     attach_function :create_client_from_uri, [
       :string,         # *const c_char (uri_str)
       :string,         # *const c_char (extra_options_json)
diff --git a/test/unit/connection_gvl_test.rb b/test/unit/connection_gvl_test.rb
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6111b3e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/test/unit/connection_gvl_test.rb
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+# frozen_string_literal: true
+
+require "test_helper"
+require "socket"
+
+# Regression test for issue #309: `Valkey.new` must release the GVL while the
+# native `create_client_from_uri` call waits on the network, so unrelated Ruby
+# threads keep running. Runs without a Valkey server: a local TCP listener
+# completes the TCP handshake but never answers, so the native connect blocks
+# until `connect_timeout` expires.
+class TestConnectionGvlUnit < Minitest::Test
+  def test_client_creation_releases_gvl_while_connecting
+    server = TCPServer.new("127.0.0.1", 0)
+    port = server.addr[1]
+    ticks = 0
+    running = true
+    ticker = Thread.new do
+      while running
+        ticks += 1
+        sleep 0.005
+      end
+    end
+    sleep 0.05 # let the ticker start
+
+    ticks_before = ticks
+    started = Process.clock_gettime(Process::CLOCK_MONOTONIC)
+    assert_raises(Valkey::CannotConnectError) do
+      Valkey.new(host: "127.0.0.1", port: port, connect_timeout: 0.5, timeout: 0.5)
+    end
+    elapsed = Process.clock_gettime(Process::CLOCK_MONOTONIC) - started
+    ticks_during = ticks - ticks_before
+
+    assert_operator elapsed, :>=, 0.2, "native connect returned too fast (#{elapsed}s) to observe GVL behaviour"
+    assert_operator ticks_during, :>=, 10,
+                    "only #{ticks_during} ticker iterations ran during a #{elapsed.round(2)}s connect; " \
+                    "create_client_from_uri appears to hold the GVL"
+  ensure
+    running = false
+    ticker&.join
+    server&.close
+  end
+end
